# Copy to android/keystore.properties and fill in. That file is gitignored:
# the upload key signs every future version of this app and cannot be rotated
# casually — whoever holds it can publish as us.
#
# storeFile is resolved relative to android/, so a key sitting beside this file
# is just its filename — but DON'T put it there. An absolute path pointing
# outside the repo is what you want: `*.keystore` is gitignored, and a
# gitignored file in a working tree is exactly what `git clean -xfd` deletes
# without naming. That is the likeliest end of this app's first upload key.
# See docs/play-store.md §1.
#
#   storeFile=C:/dev/keys/bourbon-cup-upload.keystore
#
# Forward slashes, or doubled backslashes — this is a Java properties file.
#
# Every value here can be given as an environment variable instead, which is
# what CI should do: BC_KEYSTORE_FILE, BC_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD, BC_KEY_ALIAS,
# BC_KEY_PASSWORD. The environment wins over this file.
#
# Create one with — all on one line, because a `\` continuation is bash and a
# parse error in PowerShell, which is where this gets pasted:
#   keytool -genkey -v -keystore C:/dev/keys/bourbon-cup-upload.keystore -alias bourbon-cup -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 -validity 10000
#
# (macOS/Linux: any path outside the repo — ~/keys/bourbon-cup-upload.keystore.)
#
# Left BLANK on purpose rather than pre-filled with a filename: a placeholder
# path that does not exist fails later and reads like a mistake you made,
# where a blank one fails immediately with the message that tells you what to
# create.
storeFile=
storePassword=
keyAlias=bourbon-cup
keyPassword=
